SUSPECTED BUG: call site of json.Unmarshal(data, &w) in parse.Request (stdlib + reflection + dynamic calls; large).
Run-time truth for the wireTransfer target: *json.SyntaxError and *json.UnmarshalTypeError only. A static answer
may add encoding/json's other origins (InvalidUnmarshalError, semantic and syntactic errors, time and strconv errors of
types that are never decoded here) and Unresolved entries for reflection; that over-approximation is accepted.
Compare parse_request_decl, where none of these origins leaves Request.
Actual: 158 entries, among them sentinel example.com/bank/domain.ErrLimitExceeded (bare and behind
(*json.UnmarshalTypeError).Unwrap), which json.Unmarshal can never return. It comes from errors.Unwrap(err) in
encoding/json.transformSyntacticError: the u.Unwrap() call inside errors.Unwrap is resolved to all 14 Unwrap
methods of the program, including (*limits.Exceeded).Unwrap, which returns that sentinel, instead of unwrapping
the values of the argument.
-- args --
parse/parse.go:@unmarshal_call
